DESCRIPTION:Dale Elliott Jr. is a Jamaican-American comedian\, actor\, and 
 digital powerhouse who has sold over 20\,000 tickets worldwide and is fresh
  off his acclaimed Son of an Immigrant World Tour. In just three years\, Da
 le has headlined three major comedy tours — Problem Child\, No Hard Feeli
 ngs\, and Son of an Immigrant — selling out theaters across the United St
 ates\, Canada\, and Europe. Now\, after three successful tours that helped 
 establish him as one of the fastest-rising independent comedians in the gam
 e\, Dale Elliott Jr. returns bigger\, sharper\, and more experienced with h
 is brand-new tour: Funny How Life Works. This new hour dives into the unpre
 dictable journey of chasing success\, navigating relationships\, cultural i
 dentity\, and the unexpected twists that prove life can be both chaotic and
  hilarious.\n\nWith over 1 million followers across social media\, Dale has
  built a fiercely loyal global audience by blending sharp stand-up\, cultur
 al storytelling\, and authentic humor rooted in the immigrant experience. H
 is comedy has resonated with fans across continents\, helping him grow from
  viral sensation to a consistent theater-selling headliner.\n\nBorn and rai
 sed in Jamaica\, Dale moved to Los Angeles at just 23 years old\, where he 
 independently built his comedy career from the ground up. Although he only 
 began pursuing stand-up comedy three years ago\, his rise has been nothing 
 short of remarkable. Beyond stand-up\, Dale is also the lead actor in the f
 eature film Sprinter\, showcasing his growing presence as a multifaceted en
 tertainer with crossover appeal in film\, live entertainment\, and digital 
 media.\n\nDriven\, self-made\, and unapologetically authentic\, Dale Elliot
 t Jr. represents the new generation of comedians — artists who own their 
 audience\, their voice\, and their vision.\n\nCouple's Package includes:\n\
 n- 2 premium seats\n- $90 food & beverage credit ($45 per person)\n- Gratui
 ty\n- Ticket Protection\n\nManagement reserves the right to prevent custome
 rs from entering the facility who they…\nMore info: https://comedyatlas.a
 pp/comedy-atlas/event/special-event-dale-elliott-jr/
